## Goal
Make the CI workflow that posts the gitreason comment on PRs stop blocking them when the gitreason release can't be downloaded: skip the step and emit a warning instead of failing.

## Problems
The token available to the consuming repo can't download releases of the private gitreason repo ("release not found"), so the comment job failed and blocked PR #1. The third Claude review run's wait command exited with failure, so its output had to be inspected by hand. The Codex review couldn't run Go tests because the environment was read-only.

## Decision
Edit the gitreason workflow so a failed release download turns into a skipped comment with a warning, until gitreason supports a dedicated token. This keeps PRs mergeable while the release is private, without removing the job. Before pushing, the change went through cross-review: Codex found no regressions and a security review approved. After the push, the Claude review reported no blocking findings and the claude-review check passed. A follow-up edit to the workflow's explanatory comment was then started.

